From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: force S16_LE on PSC — MTK driver lies about FLOAT support

The MT8167 ALSA driver returns 0 (success) from
snd_pcm_hw_params_test_format() for SND_PCM_FORMAT_FLOAT, but then
rejects the committed hw_params with EINVAL.  RetroArch's alsa_init_pcm
has no retry path after that failure, so audio init fails entirely.

Force SND_PCM_FORMAT_S16 unconditionally for this PSC build.  The PSC
has no use case that benefits from float samples, and S16 is confirmed
working with the MTK driver.
---
 audio/common/alsa.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/common/alsa.c b/audio/common/alsa.c
index 7f6ba13..3519275 100644
--- a/audio/common/alsa.c
+++ b/audio/common/alsa.c
@@ -74,9 +74,10 @@ int alsa_init_pcm(snd_pcm_t **pcm,
       goto error;
    }

-   format = (snd_pcm_hw_params_test_format(*pcm, params, SND_PCM_FORMAT_FLOAT) == 0)
-         ? SND_PCM_FORMAT_FLOAT : SND_PCM_FORMAT_S16;
-   stream_info->has_float = (format == SND_PCM_FORMAT_FLOAT);
+   /* PSC MTK audio driver reports SND_PCM_FORMAT_FLOAT as supported via
+    * test_format but rejects it with EINVAL in snd_pcm_hw_params. Force S16. */
+   format = SND_PCM_FORMAT_S16;
+   stream_info->has_float = false;

    RARCH_LOG("[ALSA] Using %s sample format for %s device \"%s\".\n",
          snd_pcm_format_name(format),
